    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP is anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (85.08) and **Josh Naylor** (77.77), both of whom benefit significantly from facing favorable SP_xERA matchups. **Corbin Carroll** is the standout play, as the combination of an elite matchup against Zack Littell and a prime #3 lineup slot creates a massive ceiling, even with a minor efficiency tax for the opponent's ability to hold runners. Joining him, **James Wood** (73.03) provides a high-floor, high-upside play at the top of his lineup; his elite 0.401 xwOBA against Eduardo Rodriguez makes him nearly untouchable in today\u2019s configuration. \n\nThe lineup leans heavily into environmental factors, specifically wind and park effects. **Brice Turang** (71.16) and **Jose Caballero** (67.57) are key beneficiaries of wind-out conditions and favorable park factors, which elevate their production potential despite varied strength in their respective pitching matchups. We have opted to bench **Austin Riley** (43.87) in favor of these options; while he technically cleared our 40-point threshold for potential inclusion, he remains a marginal play compared to the higher efficiency ratings provided by our starters. His downgrade is primarily driven by a difficult SP_xERA from Graham Ashcraft and a suboptimal spot in the batting order.\n\nSeveral flags remain for the manager to monitor as we approach first pitch. We are currently tracking \"Lineup Pending\" status for key starters including **Dalton Rushing**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Brice Turang**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Alex Freeland**, **Jose Caballero**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **James Wood**, and **Corbin Carroll**. Any late-breaking news regarding lineup placement could force a re-evaluation of these efficiency scores, particularly for those hitting in the lower third of the order. Additionally, while **Mickey Moniak** and **Giancarlo Stanton** are currently rostered, they remain unavailable due to IL status, further limiting our ability to pivot should weather or late scratches impact the current projections.",
